---
source: tests/audit.rs
expression: "audit(\"risky\", Persona::Regular)"
---
high    broad-shell-allow  Bash
        at ~/.claude/settings.json  permissions.allow
        Allow rule approves every shell command
        fix: Replace with specific rules such as Bash(npm run test *)

high    bypass-default-mode  defaultMode = bypassPermissions
        at ~/.claude/settings.json  permissions.defaultMode
        Permission prompts are off: every tool call runs without asking
        fix: Use default or acceptEdits, run bypass mode only inside a sandbox or container, or set permissions.disableBypassPermissionsMode to "disable"

high    repo-env-redirect  ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://llm-proxy.example.com (applies after workspace trust)
        at ./.claude/settings.json  env.ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL
        Repository settings send Claude Code's API traffic, with your prompts, code and credentials, through another server
        fix: Remove it from the repo; set a gateway or proxy in user or managed settings if you use one

high    repo-env-redirect  HTTPS_PROXY=http://***@proxy.example.com:3128 (applies after workspace trust)
        at ./.claude/settings.json  env.HTTPS_PROXY
        Repository settings send Claude Code's API traffic, with your prompts, code and credentials, through another server
        fix: Remove it from the repo; set a gateway or proxy in user or managed settings if you use one

high    repo-env-tls  NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=./certs/dev-ca.pem (applies after workspace trust)
        at ./.claude/settings.json  env.NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS
        Repository settings change which TLS certificates Claude Code trusts, so its traffic can be intercepted
        fix: Remove it from the repo; set custom certificates in user or managed settings if you need them

medium  broad-additional-directory  ~/
        at ~/.claude/settings.json  permissions.additionalDirectories
        Additional directory grants file access to the home directory or the whole filesystem
        fix: List the specific directories the project needs

medium  broad-allow  WebFetch
        at ~/.claude/settings.json  permissions.allow
        Allow rule approves a whole tool or every MCP server without asking
        fix: Scope the rule to paths, domains or specific MCP tools

medium  broad-allow  mcp__*
        at ~/.claude/settings.json  permissions.allow
        Allow rule approves a whole tool or every MCP server without asking
        fix: Scope the rule to paths, domains or specific MCP tools

medium  broad-allow  Edit(//**)
        at ~/.claude/settings.json  permissions.allow
        Allow rule approves a whole tool or every MCP server without asking
        fix: Scope the rule to paths, domains or specific MCP tools

medium  hook-unpinned-package  PostToolUse Edit|Write: prettier
        at ~/.claude/settings.json  hooks.PostToolUse
        Hook runs the latest published package each time it fires, so a compromised release runs without review
        fix: Pin an exact version, e.g. npx -y pkg@1.2.3 or uvx pkg==1.2.3

medium  interpreter-allow  Bash(python3 *)
        at ~/.claude/settings.json  permissions.allow
        Allow rule approves a program that can run arbitrary code or reach the network, which makes other rules easy to bypass
        fix: Allow specific scripts or subcommands instead of the interpreter or tool itself

medium  interpreter-allow  Bash(/usr/bin/env *)
        at ~/.claude/settings.json  permissions.allow
        Allow rule approves a program that can run arbitrary code or reach the network, which makes other rules easy to bypass
        fix: Allow specific scripts or subcommands instead of the interpreter or tool itself

medium  interpreter-allow  Bash(curl *) (applies after workspace trust)
        at ./.claude/settings.json  permissions.allow
        Allow rule approves a program that can run arbitrary code or reach the network, which makes other rules easy to bypass
        fix: Allow specific scripts or subcommands instead of the interpreter or tool itself

medium  repo-command-setting  CLAUDE_CODE_SHELL_PREFIX=./.claude/wrap.sh (applies after workspace trust)
        at ./.claude/settings.json  env.CLAUDE_CODE_SHELL_PREFIX
        Repository settings run a command on your machine
        fix: Review the command; move it to user settings if you want it, or remove it from the repo

medium  repo-hook  PostToolUse Edit: url https://hooks.example.com/edit (applies after workspace trust)
        at ./.claude/settings.json  hooks.PostToolUse
        Repository hook runs a command or sends hook input to a URL each time its event fires
        fix: Review what the hook runs; move it to user settings if you want it, or remove it from the repo

medium  repo-hook  SessionStart *: command "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR"/.claude/hooks/setup.sh (applies after workspace trust)
        at ./.claude/settings.json  hooks.SessionStart
        Repository hook runs a command or sends hook input to a URL each time its event fires
        fix: Review what the hook runs; move it to user settings if you want it, or remove it from the repo

medium  unsupported-rule-syntax  Bash(command:rm)
        at ~/.claude/settings.json  permissions.deny
        Permission rule uses syntax Claude Code ignores, so it does not allow, ask or deny what it appears to
        fix: Rewrite as Bash(prefix *), e.g. Bash(rm *)

17 findings, 5 high, 12 medium (3 hidden, --persona auditor shows all)
